  "run": {
    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "## Household review complete\n\nI submitted four approved requests:\n\n- **Pinecrest Hardware:** $75.11 refund request for return PH-20819; request PH-1001.\n- **CloudBox:** $29.97 for three $9.99 charges after the July 28 cancellation; case CB-1002. The plan was already cancelled.\n- **Summit Card:** $19.07 reversal request for four foreign transaction fees; message SC-1003.\n- **StreamFlix:** Asked about loyalty pricing after the monthly price rose from $15.99 to $18.99; ticket SF-1004. No plan change was authorized. Returning to the old price would save about $36 per year.\n\nFollow-ups are scheduled for **October 20** for Summit and **October 24** for Pinecrest, CloudBox, and StreamFlix.\n\nShopMart\u2019s promised **$43.95** refund posted September 11, so no request was needed. Spotify\u2019s $11.99 monthly charge and Oakview Apartments\u2019 rent charge appeared in the recurring inventory; I found no note saying either was unwanted. No Pinecrest refund or CloudBox post-cancellation credit appeared in the transaction records.",
    "committed_micros": 55286
  },
  "verify_run": {
    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "The new activity shows four matching credits, all posted October 15:\n\n- Pinecrest: $75.11 refund for return PH-20819\n- Summit Card: $19.07 fee reversal\n- CloudBox: $29.97 refund for post-cancellation charges\n- StreamFlix: $9.00 loyalty credit for three months of the price increase\n\nI recorded each as received with the transaction and reply as evidence. ShopMart\u2019s $43.95 return refund had already posted September 11.\n\nThe recurring inventory also shows Spotify at $11.99/month and Oakview Apartments rent at $1,550/month. I found no note saying these are unwanted, so I took no cancellation action. No additional open review items remain.",
    "committed_micros": 14991
